// Ship sidecar v1 — the protocol every Tier 1+ isolation backend speaks
// to its host. Same wire whether the sidecar runs in:
//
//   - a local Docker container (Tier 2 — DockerEngine)
//   - a local youki rootless container (Tier 2 — YoukiRootless)
//   - a local microVM (Tier 3 — LimaVm)
//   - a Fly machine or other vendor sandbox (Tier 4 — FlyMachines)
//
// One contract; the host adapts the transport (unix socket / vsock /
// TCP+TLS) to the deployment.
//
// ## Versioning
//
// Package is `ship.sidecar.v1`. Wire path is
// `/ship.sidecar.v1.<Service>/<Method>`. Field numbers are stable.
// Additive changes (new fields, new methods, new enum values with
// the `_UNSPECIFIED = 0` sentinel) are backwards compatible — old
// hosts ignore unknown fields; old sidecars return error if asked for
// a method they don't implement.
//
// Breaking changes go through `ship.sidecar.v2` with an overlap
// window. Sidecars MUST report their `protocol_version` in
// `Handshake` so the host knows whether to talk v1 or fall through.

